      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hello again, just tested the open beta and created a cross-compatible world just for haptics testing because of some concerns over the strength.\n<SNIPPED, SEE COMMENT ABOVE>\nI have noted several things from testing with Vive wands, Index controllers & Quest controllers:\n-Quest's default vibration is like 10x stronger, just from booting up the tutorial and having the prompt to move (couldn't test the map because Quest doesn't have an open beta).\nI think tweaking the values way up and therefore allowing world creators to have a better control of how hard they can vibrate the controllers would be amazing, there is so much that can be done through haptics and the controllers can definitely output so, so much more than this, it could even make vibrations usable as a game mechanic! (cough cough, totally not saying that for my spookality world cough)\nAnyway, thank you very much!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5f65e71bd9c2082619616b0a",
      "author": {
