        {
          "_id": "5f3cf7361b136917b119d507",
          "alias": "Mandarin Kite",
          "aliasID": "65c27aabed6eefce4c6e0246",
          "anonymized": false,
          "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/846a8681bdf302e2af4e3e17051ec143.png",
          "created": "2020-08-19T09:56:06.909Z",
          "name": "Yodokoro",
          "serviceAccount": false,
          "urlName": null
        }
      ],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5e95495b547d220f5c84e907",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 8
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "After some findings by @{5f3cf7361b136917b119d507|full_name} and with the newest version finally out (including the return of UI buttons) I've updated the map to make it a better test case:\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_7f010f63-7a82-4668-b1a5-412b57fb08f5&instanceId=0\nIt is now much simpler to use with three sliders:\n-Duration slider from 0 to 5 seconds\n-Amplitude slider from 0 to 1\n-Frequency slider from 0 to 320\nOne button to vibrate the controllers once according to the sliders.\nOne toggle to enable a \"continuous\" mode that'll time it so a vibration happens after the currently set Duration has finished.\nFor the findings (only tested on Vive wands as of current):\n-Amplitude is still 0-1 but after comparing it with a purely SteamVR project (I can try to package it if needed), we are probably getting about 10%(?) of the actual possible amplitude.\n-Frequency does seem to be from 0 to 320, but from @{5f3cf7361b136917b119d507|full_name} findings and current experience, it seems to cap at 100 in VRChat (for Vive anyway)\nNow after going all out on the SteamVR project, I can definitely understand that there needs to be limits (with a strong enough, long vibration, it's possible to have the controllers lose tracking for example), but still, I feel like we should be able to harness much, much more of that haptic power.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
